(LST-18 — appending an OPAQUE value (a function with no declared return
 type) widens the list to mixed. LANGUAGE.md:2232-2235 says the element is
 then "always read back as what it is rather than silently reinterpreted".
 It is not: an opaque function returning a TEXT lands in the slot tagged as
 a number and prints as a raw address (4210906, deterministic).
 Also covers: LST-21 (the residual TAG_INTEGER guess of
 LANGUAGE.md:2250-2254 — this probe is what that hedge looks like in
 practice). See Discrepancy 5; minimal repro `D5.vox`.
